g older adults</article-title><source>Prev Chronic Dis</source><fpage>A14</fpage><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/pcd/issues/2008/jan/07_0148.htm">http://www.cdc.gov/pcd/issues/2008/jan/07_0148.htm</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18082003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shenson</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Benson</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><volume>5</volume><issue>1</issue><article-title>Expanding the delivery of clinical preventive services through community collaboration: the SPARC model</article-title><source>Prev Chronic Dis</source><fpage>A20</fpage><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/pcd/issues/2008/jan/07_0139.htm">http://www.cdc.gov/pcd/issues/2008/jan/07_0139.htm</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18082009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Friedman</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Kao</surname><given-names>EK</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><volume>5</volume><issue>1</issue><article-title>A Comprehensive Assessment of the Difficulty Level and Cultural Sensitivity of Online Cancer Prevention Resources for Older Minority Men</article-title><source>Prev Chronic Dis</source><fpage>A07</fpage><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/pcd/issues/2008/jan/07_0146.htm">http://www.cdc.gov/pcd/issues/2008/jan/07_0146.htm</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18081996</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aldrich</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Benson</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><volume>5</volume><issue>1</issue><article-title>Disaster Preparedness and the Chronic Disease Needs of Vulnerable Older Adults</article-title><source>Prev Chronic Dis</source><fpage>A27</fpage><comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/pcd//issues/2008/jan/07_0135.htm">http://www.cdc.gov/pcd//issues/2008/jan/07_0135.htm</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18082016</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn><p>The opinions expressed by authors contributing to this journal do not necessarily reflect the opinions of the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, the Public Health Service, Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, or the authors' affiliated institutions. Use of trade names is for identification only and does not imply endorsement by any of the groups named above.</p></fn><fn><p>					<italic>Suggested citation for this article:</italic> Rao JK. Looking back and looking forward.  Prev Chronic Dis 2008:5(1). <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/pcd/issues/2008/jan/07_0179.htm">http://www.cdc.gov/pcd/issues/2008/jan/07_0179.htm</ext-link>. Accessed [<italic>date</italic>].				</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>